WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
A ticker is only the beginning.
Start with AAPL. A generated example—not a market observation.

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:15.000
Change the question of time.
Use the real range control to inspect three months.

3
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:26.000
Give performance a reference point.
AAPL against SPY. Generated returns on shared example dates.

4
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Understand the return. And the risk.
Period return. Excess vs SPY. Volatility. Maximum drawdown.

5
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:46.000
See what the numbers mean.
Open the methodology. Inspect the reasoning, not just the result.

6
00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:52.000
Keep the context. Keep your judgment.
Stockbear · Research, not investment advice.
